   454	def _identity_of(location: str) -> Identity | None:
   455	    """What filesystem object this path names right now, or None if it is absent.
   456	
   457	    The split is between an ANSWER and an unanswered question, and the two used
   458	    to be one branch. A path that does not exist genuinely names no object —
   459	    that is None, and it is correct, and the mint path depends on it. A path
   460	    that DOES exist and will not stat (a permission wall, a transient I/O
   461	    error, a partially mounted volume) leaves the question open, and answering
   462	    None there means a store replaced under an aliased spelling opens as first
   463	    contact.
